From 664a23cfa9ce20c78bf8c244518ea25431103000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Code (independent review)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:26:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Revise M4 proposal (R2): tolerance floor, finite partial
 integrals, inversion exits

Address the three blocking findings of the independent R1 review:
- F1: effective tolerance floor 1024 MIN_VALUE; B5 split into an unconditional
  part (constant computed speed) and an explicit condition; 8 K MIN_VALUE
  underflow term in the rounding allowance.
- F2: ratio mode only for 1/2 <= I2/I1 <= 2, linear fallback otherwise;
  F_k is never NaN and lies in [0, I2_k].
- F3: Newton for at most 16 iterations, then bisection; proven bracket bound
  2^-47 (b - a) + 2 ulp; cap and collapse exits return the better bracket end
  (ties to hi); work bound 336 derivative evaluations (was 400).

Adds M4R2RegressionTest (9 tests); no test removed. Reference data unchanged.
No production code; M1, M2 and M3 untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
